package main;

// A standard root that does not exist is diagnosed only when an import needs
// it (m6a-plan decision "Package-root precedence"). This program never names
// `core:`, so a compiler installed without that component still builds it —
// which is also why it cannot print: `core:fmt` lives under the root this case
// deliberately points at nothing.

main :: proc() { assert(3 == 3); }
